# health v2.9 — WARNING. health:allergenCode carrying a STRING LITERAL where an
# IRI belongs.
#
# WHY A LITERAL AND NOT A WRONG IRI. health:allergenCode carries no sh:pattern
# and no sh:maxCount, deliberately: SNOMED CT identifiers, RxNorm concept
# identifiers and UNII codes have unrelated lexical formats, so any pattern
# would reject valid codes, and CodeableConcept.coding is 0..* so any maxCount
# would reject dual coding. sh:nodeKind sh:IRI is therefore the ONLY constraint
# the property carries, and a bare literal is the only thing that can violate
# it. A fixture using a malformed IRI would assert nothing, because the shape
# does not inspect an IRI's shape and must not.
#
# This is also the realistic failure rather than an invented one. A converter
# reading FHIR sees code.coding[].code as a JSON string, "7980", and the whole
# work of emitting this property is joining that string to code.coding[].system
# to build the code system's IRI. Skipping that join is the natural mistake, and
# it produces exactly this record: a value that looks like the code, in the
# right predicate, that no consumer can resolve or join against any other
# vocabulary. The record still has its display text, so nothing about it reads
# as broken.
#
# sh:Warning, not sh:Violation, per the core v3.5 ratchet: this is the first
# release in which health:allergenCode exists at all. Nothing rejects this
# record, and the fixture asserts exactly that alongside the warning.
#
# Fully synthetic.

@prefix cascade: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/core/v1#> .
@prefix clinical: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/clinical/v1#> .
@prefix health: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/health/v1#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<urn:uuid:a11e0209-0000-4000-8000-000000000004> a health:AllergyRecord ;
    health:allergen "Penicillin G" ;
    health:allergenCode "7980" ;
    health:allergyCategory "medication" ;
    health:reaction "Hives" ;
    health:allergySeverity "severe" ;
    clinical:criticality "high" ;
    clinical:allergyType "allergy" ;
    clinical:status "active" ;
    clinical:sourceEHR "Meridian Health System" ;
    cascade:dataProvenance cascade:EHRVerified ;
    cascade:schemaVersion "1.4" .
